{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>The sister of Aaron.</b> It seems correct in my eyes that because Moses and Miriam were mentioned in the Song and Aaron was not mentioned, Scripture wished to mention him, and it said <b>the sister of Aaron</b> as an expression of honor for him — for he is her older brother, and his sister the prophetess traces her lineage to him, for he too is a prophet and a holy one of HaShem. And it is also possible that it is the way of Scripture to trace lineage to the greatest of the brothers, as in \"and the sons of Caleb the brother of Jerahmeel\" (1 Chronicles 2:42), for he was greater than his brothers, as it is stated (1 Chronicles 2:9), \"Jerahmeel, and Ram, and Chelubai.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The closing biblical quotation in the Hebrew omits the word את before ירחמאל, but I have supplied it to match the verse being cited."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:08:46.207012873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}